@@ ============================================================
@@ GAssist — gravity-assist (swing-by): deflection & free ΔV, patched-conic
@@ In the planet frame v∞ keeps its magnitude and turns by δ, sin(δ/2)=1/e, e=1+rp·v∞²/μ.
@@ Free Δv = 2·v∞/e (exact, no trig), maximal near v∞ ≈ √(μ/rp).
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ Input  : v∞ r_p μ   ( v∞ r_p μ -- { δ Δv e } )
@@ Output : { δ Δv e } — deflection (°), free Δv (m/s), hyperbola e
@@ VALIDATION (device-confirmed):
@@   5_km/s 3500_km ⒸGM♂ GAssist -> { 38.36995_° 3286.18964_m/s 3.04304 }
@@   13.973_km/s 3500_km ⒸGM♂ GAssist -> { 6.76222_° 1648.17768_m/s 16.95570 }
@@ ============================================================
 → vinf rp μ
  «
    DEG
    vinf UBASE Uval 'vinf' STO  rp UBASE Uval 'rp' STO  μ UBASE Uval 'μ' STO
    '1+rp·vinf^2/μ' EVAL → ecc
    «
      '2·ASIN(1/ecc)' EVAL
      '2·vinf/ecc' EVAL  1_m/s ·
      ecc
      3 →LIST
    »
  »
